# This is the CONCEPT DOI: it always resolves to the latest version, so it stays
# correct across releases. It deliberately is not a version DOI. A version DOI is
# minted by Zenodo only after the tag is pushed, so a version DOI can never be
# present in the CITATION.cff that the release itself archives -- v2.0.1's archive
# carries the v2.0.0 values for exactly that reason.
#
# The version DOI of the release behind the first revision of ms. 3395422 is
# 10.5281/zenodo.22235209 (v2.0.1). That number lives in the manuscript's Data
# Availability Statement and in the Supporting Information README, and those are
# the places to change it when a new release is cut.
